 Prince Prospero to seal himself and a thousand courtiers within a fortified, elaborately designed abbey to escape the contagion. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, except the western chamber, which is shrouded in black velvet and blood-red glass—host a lavish masked ball filled with grotesque revelers, music, and wine. As the night progresses, the ominous ebony clock in the black room chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread, until at midnight, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, appears and stalks through the rooms. Enraged, Prince Prospero pursues the figure with a dagger, but the intruder turns in the black chamber, and the prince collapses dead; the revelers rush in only to find the mask empty, realizing the Red Death itself has infiltrated their sanctuary, and one by one, all die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"characters\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\\\",\\n      \\\"canonical_name\\\": \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\",\\n      \\\"aliases\\\": [\\n        \\\"the mummer\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"role\\\": null,\\n      \\\"appearance\\\": null,\\n      \\\"personality\\\": null,\\n      \\\"voice_guidance\\\": null,\\n      \\\"descriptions\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"text\\\": \\\"Prince Prospero is a bold and robust man who presides over a lavish, isolated gathering of revellers. He initially reacts with rage and indignation to the intrusion of a masked figure dressed as the Red Death, but later pursues the intruder with fury before being fatally struck and killed in the black chamber.\\\",\\n          \\\"source_position\\\": 10339,\\n          \\\"chapter_index\\\": null,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"llm_refined\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"relationships\\\": {},\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Prince Prospero is described as bold and robust\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"the prince was a bold and robust man\\\",\\n          \\\"position\\\": 11148,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"statement\\\": \\\"He reacts with anger and demands the intruder be seized\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\\\",\\n          \\\"position\\\": 11148,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"statement\\\": \\\"He pursues the intruder through the chambers in a state of rage\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers\\\",\\n          \\\"position\\\": 12389,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"statement\\\": \\\"He is fatally stabbed by the intruder in the black chamber\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\\\",\\n          \\\"position\\\": 12980,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"statement\\\": \\\"He is killed while confronting the masked intruder in the black chamber\\\",\\n          \\\"quote\\\": \\\"afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\\\",\\n          \\\"position\\\": 13136,\\n          \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"voice_notes\\\": null,\\n      \\\"first_appearance_chapter\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"mention_count\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"is_narrator\\\": false,\\n      \\\"narrative_role\\\": null\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"pronunciations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"word\\\": \\\"Prospero\\\",\\n      \\\"flag_reason\\\": \\\"proper_noun\\\",\\n      \\\"occurrences\\\": 18,\\n      \\\"first_position\\\": 631,\\n      \\\"chapter_indices\\\": [\\n        1\\n      ],\\n      \\\"context_examples\\\": [\\n        \\\"...izure, progress and termination of the disease, were the incidents of half an hour. But the Prince Prospero was happy and dauntless and sagacious. When his dominions were half depopulated, he summoned to his...\\\",\",\"numLines\":100,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":1588}}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01UmpdmxpZWctZ384Z2dyx2U\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perfect! I can see the issue. \\\"the mummer\\\" is listed as an alias of \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\". Let me trace this more. Let me check the text to see what the actual entities look like:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1880,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":54433,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1880,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e30197d8-bf0e-4f29-bd1c-66012b466cd3\",\"uuid\":\"936c7f52-2eb9-45db-ad94-c20482aeb1fb\"}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01UmpdmxpZWctZ384Z2dyx2U\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013tEdAtXqcYrhqULxNP6CJX\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"mummer\\\" \\\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\\\" | head -10\",\"description\":\"Find occurrences of 'mummer' in text\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1880,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":54433,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1880,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e30197d8-bf0e-4f29-bd1c-66012b466cd3\",\"uuid\":\"bbf96847-2b6d-423f-aa40-5a3e1456982e\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_013tEdAtXqcYrhqULxNP6CJX\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"22:    In an assembly of phantasms such as I have painted, it may well be supposed that no ordinary appearance could have excited such sensation. In truth the masquerade license of the night was nearly unlimited; but the figure in question had out-Heroded Herod, and gone beyond the bounds of even the prince's indefinite decorum. There are chords in the hearts of the most reckless which cannot be touched without emotion. Even with the utterly lost, to whom life and death are equally jests, there are matters of which no jest can be made. The whole company, indeed, seemed now deeply to feel that in the costume and bearing of the stranger neither wit nor propriety existed. The figure was tall and gaunt, and shrouded from head to foot in the habiliments of the grave. The mask which concealed the visage was made so nearly to resemble the countenance of a stiffened corpse that the closest scrutiny must have had difficulty in detecting the cheat. And yet all this might have been endured, if not approved, by the mad revellers around. But the mummer had gone so far as to assume the type of the Red Death. His vesture was dabbled in blood -- and his broad brow, with all the features of the face, was besprinkled with the scarlet horror. \\n30:    It was in the blue room where stood the prince, with a group of pale courtiers by his side. At first, as he spoke, there was a slight rushing movement of this group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which the mad assumptions of the mummer had inspired the whole party, there were found none who put forth hand to seize him; so that, unimpeded, he passed within a yard of the prince's person; and, while the vast assembly, as if with one impulse, shrank from the centres of the rooms to the walls, he made his way uninterruptedly, but with the same solemn and measured step which had distinguished him from the first, through the blue chamber to the purple -- through the purple to the green -- through the green to the orange -- through this again to the white -- and even thence to the violet, ere a decided movement had been made to arrest him. It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had seized upon all. He bore aloft a drawn dagger, and had approached, in rapid impetuosity, to within three or four feet of the retreating figure, when the latter, having attained the extremity of the velvet apartment, turned suddenly and confronted his pursuer. There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero. Then, summoning the wild courage of despair, a throng of the revellers at once threw themselves into the black apartment, and, seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock, gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled with so violent a rudeness, untenanted by any tangible form.\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e30197d8-bf0e-4f29-bd1c-66012b466cd3\",\"uuid\":\"d26053b9-ee6b-47f9-bac2-57c2aaab5cb2\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"22:    In an assembly of phantasms such as I have painted, it may well be supposed that no ordinary appearance could have excited such sensation. In truth the masquerade license of the night was nearly unlimited; but the figure in question had out-Heroded Herod, and gone beyond the bounds of even the prince's indefinite decorum. There are chords in the hearts of the most reckless which cannot be touched without emotion. Even with the utterly lost, to whom life and death are equally jests, there are matters of which no jest can be made. The whole company, indeed, seemed now deeply to feel that in the costume and bearing of the stranger neither wit nor propriety existed. The figure was tall and gaunt, and shrouded from head to foot in the habiliments of the grave. The mask which concealed the visage was made so nearly to resemble the countenance of a stiffened corpse that the closest scrutiny must have had difficulty in detecting the cheat. And yet all this might have been endured, if not approved, by the mad revellers around. But the mummer had gone so far as to assume the type of the Red Death. His vesture was dabbled in blood -- and his broad brow, with all the features of the face, was besprinkled with the scarlet horror. \\n30:    It was in the blue room where stood the prince, with a group of pale courtiers by his side. At first, as he spoke, there was a slight rushing movement of this group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which the mad assumptions of the mummer had inspired the whole party, there were found none who put forth hand to seize him; so that, unimpeded, he passed within a yard of the prince's person; and, while the vast assembly, as if with one impulse, shrank from the centres of the rooms to the walls, he made his way uninterruptedly, but with the same solemn and measured step which had distinguished him from the first, through the blue chamber to the purple -- through the purple to the green -- through the green to the orange -- through this again to the white -- and even thence to the violet, ere a decided movement had been made to arrest him. It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had seized upon all. He bore aloft a drawn dagger, and had approached, in rapid impetuosity, to within three or four feet of the retreating figure, when the latter, having attained the extremity of the velvet apartment, turned suddenly and confronted his pursuer. There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero. Then, summoning the wild courage of despair, a throng of the revellers at once threw themselves into the black apartment, and, seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock, gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled with so violent a rudeness, untenanted by any tangible form.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_01XjL5CxjgUSHGoKqzCfHXbd\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perfect! Now I can see the text. Let me check:\\n1. \\\"the mummer\\\" - lowercase \\\"m\\\" (epithet)\\n2. \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" - capitalized words (proper name)\\n\\nSo \\\"the mummer\\\" should be classified as an epithet, and \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" as a proper name. They should go through cross-group resolution. But why are they being merged?\\n\\nLet me add diagnostic logging to understand what's happening. But first, let me check the latest logs to see if there's already l